<div class="sect1">
<h2 id="Application_Layer"><a class="anchor" href="#Application_Layer"></a>Application Layer</h2>
<div class="sectionbody">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Application oriented errors are returned as HTTP status <code>200</code> and will always be accompanied by more details in the response to the JSON message.</p>
</div>
<div class="sect2">
<h3 id="_error_structure"><a class="anchor" href="#_error_structure"></a>Error Structure</h3>
<div class="ulist">
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>timestamp</code>: Provides the exact point in time, expressed in UTC, when the response was generated.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>errors</code>: An array listing detailed error information. Each item in the array is an <code>Error</code> object.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sect2">
<h3 id="_error_object_2"><a class="anchor" href="#_error_object_2"></a>Error Object</h3>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>The <code>Error</code> object contains the following parameters:</p>
</div>
<div class="ulist">
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>category</code>: A high-level grouping of errors indicating what kind of (client-side or server-side) problem occurred.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>type</code>: An application-specific error type, or one from the list of typical Sabre API errors.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>description</code>: A human-readable description of what went wrong with enough information that a software developer can use to debug the problem.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>fieldName</code>: Additional information to help debug the error. For example, the name of a parameter missing from a request payload.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>fieldPath</code>: Additional information to help debug the error. For example, the name of a parameter missing from a request payload.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>fieldValue</code>: The source of the error.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sect2">
<h3 id="Bad_Request"><a class="anchor" href="#Bad_Request"></a>Category: BAD_REQUEST</h3>
<table class="tableblock frame-none grid-none stretch">
<colgroup>
<col style="width: 20%;">
<col style="width: 80%;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>Type</strong></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>REQUIRED_FIELD_MISSING</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>Description</strong></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Client did not provide required data. See <code>fieldName</code> for the item expected in the <code>/flightCheck</code> request.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>Root Cause</strong></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Missing required parameter in API request.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>Solution</strong></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock">Ensure proper values are provided in the request body.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><p class="tableblock"><strong>Example</strong></p></td>
<td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"><div class="content"><div class="listingblock">
<div class="content">
<pre class="highlightjs highlight"><code class="language-JSON hljs" data-lang="JSON">{
  "errors":
